  "result": "I've looked through the site. The timetable page is built straight from `sailings.csv`, which the ferry office exports each night. Nothing in that file marks a sailing as cancelled, and the site has no warning code yet.\n\nThat matters because a nightly file can't carry news from the same day. If a 2pm sailing is called off at 11am because of weather, the site won't know until the next export. So the real question is where cancellation news would come from, and how quickly it needs to reach people.\n\nWhen a sailing gets cancelled today, what actually happens? Who decides, how does word get out, and how soon after that would you want someone looking at the site to see it?",
